WEBVTT


00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.200
The winner of a 30,000-dollar scholarship...


00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:53.610
is Miss Louisiana, Erika Schwarz.


00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:57.310
And the new Miss America
is Miss Kansas...


00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.280
<i>Tara Dawn Holland!</i>


00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.390
...scholarship...


00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.400
is Miss Louisiana, Erika Schwarz.


00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:23.940
And the new Miss America
is Miss Kansas, Tara Dawn Holland!


00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.770
<i>There are two kinds
of people in this world-</i>


00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.870
<i>winners and losers.</i>


00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.850
Inside each and every one of you...


00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.320
at the very core of your being...


00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.360
is a winner
waiting to be awakened...


00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.620
and unleashed upon the world.


00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.820
With my nine-step
"Refuse to Lose" program...


00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.730
you now have the necessary
tools and the insights...


00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.140
and the know-how to put
your losing habits behind you...


00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.500
and to go out and make
your dreams come true.


00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.610
No hesitating.


00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.450
No complaining.


00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.610
And no excuses.


00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.090
I want you to go out
in the world...


00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.020
and I want you to be winners!


00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.030
Thank you.


00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.220
Thank you.


00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.440
<i>I'm on my way.</i>


00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.680
I don't know how long.
I don't know!


00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.780
Richard, he has
nowhere else to go.


00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.230
I'm not smoking.
I'm not!


00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:55.100
Look, I'm at the hospital.
Yeah, okay. Bye.


00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:23.230
Miss Hoover?
Your brother's fine.


00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:27.030
<i>I need you to keep him away
from sharp objects-knives, scissors.</i>


00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:31.330
<i>If you have medications, depressants
in your house, keep them secure.</i>


00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.900
<i>- I'd prefer to keep him, but-
- I know. The insurance.</i>


00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.070
You want to see him?


00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.000
Hey, Frank.


00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.500
Sheryl.


00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.430
I'm so glad you're still here.


00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.540
Well, that makes one of us.


00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.740
<i>A strong low pressure
system passed across New Mexico...</i>


00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:15.040
<i>bringing with it a little moisture
that will cool things off a bit.</i>


00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:18.550
<i>We may even see a five- to 10-degree drop
in temperatures in Albuquerque.</i>


00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.120
<i>There will be no significant
accumulations of rainfall-</i>


00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.350
Do you want to talk or no?


00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:27.020
<i>- Nearly nothing, but statewide 93%-
- No.</i>


00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:40.870
Hello?


00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.880
Anyone?


00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.340
Down here.
We have you with Dwayne.


00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:56.000
<i>Dwayne, hi.
Uncle Frank's here.</i>


00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.770
He doesn't mind, Frank.
We talked.


00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.780
<i>Wha- I know. I know. But we can't have you
sleeping alone. The doctor said.</i>


00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.980
I'm sorry.
I have to insist.


00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.060
You'll get along fine.
He's really quiet.


00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.750
<i>And here's your cot.</i>


00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.930
Please, Frank.


00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.300
Please.


00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.400
Thank you.


00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:37.410
I'm gonna start dinner.


00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:39.700
You can come out
when you're settled.


00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:44.010
And, uh, just leave the door open.
That's important.


00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.960
Dwayne, honey, there's
a bucket of chicken in the car.


00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.160
Can you get it?
And, uh, I'll make a salad.


00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.500
<i>- Olive?
- Yeah?</i>


00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.500
<i>- Is Grandpa with you?
- Yeah.</i>


00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.900
<i>- What are you guys doing?
- Rehearsing.</i>


00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:09.630
<i>- Okay, well, dinner in 10 minutes.
- Okay.</i>


00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.000
- Hi.
- Hi. Frank's here.


00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:17.240
Oh, God.
Did, uh, Stan Grossman call?


00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:19.820
<i>Well, check the machine.</i>


00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.250
- Dwayne, please, come on.
The chicken. It's in the car.


00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.880
Will you set the table?
We'll do paper plates tonight.


00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:28.960
<i>Remember Olive
was runner-up in the Little Miss Sunshine?</i>


00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:33.330
<i>- Theyjust called right now-
- Hey, it's your sister!</i>


00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.870
Fuck.


00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:46.940
Hi. Richard Hoover
for Stan Grossman, please.


00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.540
Any way to reach him or-


00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.880
<i>Well, I'm just wondering
if this darn book deal is done or not.</i>


00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.980
<i>If-</i>


00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:58.490
<i>Yes.</i>


00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.720
Okay, could you please just have him
call me anytime over the weekend?


00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.920
He has my cell number.
Just to let me know we're on.


00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:09.160
Okay? Thank you. Bye.


00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.790
- So what happened with Stan Grossman?
- He's in Scottsdale.


00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.130
<i>Why didn't he call?</i>


00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.000
Will you let me
worry about this, please?


00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:20.340
Dwayne, can you check on Frank?
Tell him it's dinnertime.


00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.940
<i>Olive! Dinnertime!</i>


00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:26.950
<i>Coming!</i>


00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.360
What? Dinner?


00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.410
What, you don't talk anymore?


00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.710
<i>Why not?</i>


00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.910
<i>You can talk.
You just choose not to?</i>


00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.750
<i>Is that Nietzsche?</i>


00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:59.060
You don't speak
because of Friedrich Nietzsche.


00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.470
Far out.


00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:16.370
<i>Frank, you can sit here next to Dwayne.</i>


00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:20.680
Here's the salad, and I'm gonna run
and get Sprite for everyone.


00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:25.680
<i>Olive, come on!
Dinnertime!</i>


00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.690
<i>Okay.</i>


00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.190
So who do you hang out with?


00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:44.230
No one?


00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.550
<i>What about your family?</i>


00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.850
<i>Frank! Hey!</i>


00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:09.020
- Richard.
- Good to... see you.


00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:22.000
Let me get Olive.


00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:25.480
<i>- Olive? Dad?
- You guys, go on and start.</i>


00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.670
<i>- Let's go!
- We're coming.</i>


00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:30.680
<i>- Frank, some Sprite?
- Yes.</i>


00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.720
<i>And I want everyone to have
at least a little salad.</i>


00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.050
Thanks, Sheryl.


00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:38.060
Honey.


00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:46.330
So, Sheryl, I couldn't help noticing
Dwayne has stopped speaking.


00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:49.560
Oh, yeah, he's taken a vow of silence.


00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.760
You've taken a vow of silence?


00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:54.710
<i>Yeah. He's gonna join the Air Force Academy,
become a test pilot...</i>


00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:57.800
and he's taken a vow of silence
until he reaches that goal.


00:10:57.910 --> 00:10:59.900
<i>- You're kidding?
- Hi, Uncle Frank.</i>


00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:03.210
Oh, hey, Olive.
Wow, you're gettin' big.


00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.010
<i>Almost like a real person.</i>


00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:11.900
- What happened to your arms?
- Olive.


00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.170
<i>That's all right.
I had a little accident. I'm okay.</i>


00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.570
- How's the, uh, routine coming, honey?
- It's good.


00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.580
Yeah? When are you
gonna show it to us?


00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:20.910
I don't know.
It's up to Grandpa.


00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.540
A couple of days.
It still needs work.


00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:27.350
What's that? Chicken?
Every night it's the fuckin' chicken!


00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:31.390
- Holy God Almighty! It is possible just once-
- Dad!


00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:34.550
We could get something to eat around here
that's not the goddamn fucking chicken?


00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.290
<i>- Hey, Dad! Dad!
- I'm just sayin'-</i>


00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:40.890
<i>- Christ.
- When you want to start cooking your own food, you're welcome.</i>


00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:45.130
- At Sunset Manor, you know- - If you like
Sunset Manor, you shouldn't have got kicked out.


00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.600
<i>For God's sakes.</i>


00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:53.670
So when did you start
with the vow?


00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:58.040
<i>Been nine months, Frank.
He hasn't said a word.</i>


00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:02.950
Not one. I think it shows
tremendous discipline.


00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.250
- Richard.
- I really do.


00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:07.190
Really. I think we could
learn something from Dwayne.


00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:10.630
Dwayne has a goal.
He has a dream.


00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.290
It may not be my dream,
may not be yours...


00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:16.730
but he's pursuing it with
great conviction and focus.


00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.740
In fact, I was thinking
about the nine steps-


00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.740
Oh, for crying out loud!


00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:24.800
And how Dwayne's utilizing seven of them
in his personal quest to self-fulfillment.


00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.310
Richard, please.


00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.400
Well, I'm just saying
I've come around.


00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.540
I think he could use our support.


00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.920
How did it happen?


00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.750
- How did what happen?
- Your accident.


00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.760
Honey, here.


00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.950
<i>Oh, no, it's okay.
Unless you object.</i>


00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:47.290
No, I'm pro-honesty here.
I just think, you know, it's up to you.


00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.030
Be my guest.


00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:55.200
Olive, um, Uncle Frank
didn't really have an accident.


00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:59.970
<i>What happened was he...
tried to kill himself.</i>


00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:03.480
<i>You did? Why?</i>


00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:06.520
I'm sorry. I don't think
this is an appropriate conversation.


00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.710
Honey, let's let Uncle Frank
finish his dinner, okay? Shh.


00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:12.720
Why did you want to kill yourself?


00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:15.320
<i>No, don't answer the question, Frank.</i>


00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.860
<i>- Richard! Richard!
- He's not gonna answer the question. Frank.</i>


00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.400
- I wanted to kill myself-
- Don't listen to him.


00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.630
<i>- I was very unhappy.
- He's sick in his head.</i>


00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.130
- Richard!
- I'm sorry! I don't think it's an appropriate conversation...


00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.400
- for a seven-year-old.
- She's gonna find out anyway.


00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:31.410
- Okay.
- Go on, Frank.


00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:36.840
Why were you unhappy?


00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:40.410
Um, well, there are a lot of reasons.


00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:45.430
Mainly, though, I fell in love
with someone who didn't love me back.


00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.090
Who?


00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:50.430
<i>One of my grad students.
I was very much in love with him.</i>


00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:52.910
Him?


00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:57.340
<i>It was a boy?
You fell in love with a boy?</i>


00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.570
- Yes, I did. Very much so.
- That's silly.


00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:03.380
<i>You're right. It was silly.
It was very, very silly.</i>


00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:06.550
- There's another word for it.
- Dad.


00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:10.560
<i>- So, that's when you tried to kill yourself?
- Well, no.</i>


00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.220
The boy that I was in love with fell in love
with another man- Larry Sugarman.


00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.590
- Who's Larry Sugarman?
- Larry Sugarman is, perhaps...


00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:19.860
the second most highly regarded
Proust scholar in the U.S.


00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:23.530
- Who's number one?
- That would be me, Rich.


00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:26.040
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.


00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:28.270
So that's when.


00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.740
No. What happened was
I was a bit upset...


00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:33.140
so I said some things
that I shouldn't have said...


00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.380
<i>and I did some things
that I shouldn't have done...</i>


00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.540
and subsequently
I was fired from my job...


00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:40.820
<i>and forced to move out of my apartment
and move into a motel.</i>


00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:47.080
<i>- And that's when you tried to-
- Well, no.</i>


00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.390
Actually, all of that was okay.


00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:54.090
What happened was two days ago the
MacArthur Foundation, in its infinite wisdom...


00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:58.400
<i>awarded a genius grant
to Larry Sugarman.</i>


00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:00.770
And that's when I-


00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:03.470
<i>Decided to check out early.</i>


00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:07.140
Yes. Yes. And I failed
at that as well.


00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:11.240
<i>Olive, the important thing
to understand here...</i>


00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.580
<i>is that Uncle Frank
gave up on himself.</i>


00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:17.620
He made a series of foolish choices-
I'm sorry- and he gave up on himself...


00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:20.290
which is something winners never do.


00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:24.160
So that's the story, okay?
Now, everyone, just let's move on and, uh-


00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:28.430
<i>Is he always like this? How can you stand it?</i>


00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:32.440
Olive, tell him about your
routine while you're doing this.


00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:36.440
Okay. Little Miss Chili Pepper is
a beauty contest for everyone in Albuquerque...


00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:39.670
but you have to be six or seven
and you have to be a girl.


00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:41.940
This is our sister.


00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:43.610
- Cindy.
- Spring break.


00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:46.080
Dwayne went to see his dad
in Florida for two weeks...


00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:48.550
and Olive went to Laguna
to see her cousins.


00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:53.060
- She made it to the top of the regionals out there.
- I was in second place.


00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:55.150
Well, what do you think
your chances are?


00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.230
I think I can win,
because some of the other girls...


00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.730
<i>they've been doing it longer,
but I practice every day.</i>


00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:04.700
- Yeah. Good luck.
- Not about luck, Frank.


00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.300
<i>Luck is the name losers give
to their own failings.</i>


00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:10.240
It's about wanting to win,
willing yourself to win.


00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:13.040
- You've got to want it badder than anybody else.
- I do.


00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:15.480
<i>- Then you're gonna be a winner.
- Richard.</i>


00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:17.550
It's the truth.


00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:20.760
<i>You know, actually, there is a message
from Cindy on the machine.</i>


00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.930
Something about Little Mrs. Sunshine.


00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:26.400
<i>- What? Little Miss Sunshine?
- Yeah.</i>


00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.230
What?


00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:35.580
<i>Sheryl, it's Cindy.</i>


00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.580
Remember when Olive
was here last month?


00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.120
She was runner-up in the
regional Little Miss Sunshine?


00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:43.710
<i>Theyjust called right now and said that
the girl who won had to forfeit her crown.</i>


00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.720
I don't know why.
Something about diet pills.


00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:50.280
- Now she has a place in the state
contest in Redondo Beach!


00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:55.690
Oh, my gosh! I won!
I won! I won! I won!


00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.700
<i>- Finish your dinner!
- I'm finished!</i>


00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.430
- What happened?
- I'm just calling to- Cindy!


00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:04.770
Yeah, we just got it.
Yeah, she basically went crazy.


00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.540
<i>- I won! I won! I won!
- No, I didn't get that.</i>


00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:11.810
<i>The machine cut you off. Okay.</i>


00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:15.320
<i>Redondo Beach. This Sunday?</i>


00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:19.480
<i>- Wh-Are you guys going?
- Yes.</i>


00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:22.720
- Can you put it off?
- They have to. They have to.


00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:25.460
- Where does that leave us?
- We can't do it. We can't.


00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:28.290
No, no- No, I understand
that, Cindy. Yeah.


00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.890
- They- - I just- No, I'll just
figure it out. Okay, bye-bye.


00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.940
It's this Sunday?
Why can'tJeff and Cindy take her?


00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:37.070
They have some equestrian
thing in Santa Barbara.


00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:39.910
You know, they do that horse
shit every single weekend.


00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:43.670
Well, it's the nationals. They're taking
both horses, so apparently it's a big deal.


00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:46.270
What about Olive?


00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:51.520
Little Miss Sunshine!
Little Miss Sunshine! I won!


00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.820
I won!


00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:56.020
I'm going! We're going!


00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.530
- You promised?
- We'll fly out and come back Monday.


00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:01.100
- How are you gonna get around out there?
- We'll rent a car.


00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:03.690
- And stay at a hotel?
- We can afford it.


